    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_2f0f364c",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: hateful; overall-intent-description: The meme depicts a scene where a man in a suit is being threatened by two armed individuals, with text overlaying the image. The top text reads 'how muslims see us staring down the barrel of a .45......' and the bottom text reads 'how we see muslims.' This visual and textual juxtaposition uses a violent, threatening scenario to portray Muslims as dangerous or violent, which is a harmful and hateful stereotype. The meme relies on the association of Muslims with terrorism and violence, which is a well-documented form of Islamophobia. The intent is to provoke fear and reinforce negative perceptions of Muslims by equating them with armed threats, thereby contributing to a hostile and discriminatory atmosphere. The meme is designed to incite prejudice and hostility toward Muslims by using violent imagery and false equivalencies.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_b94aff16"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
